From 41ee974d0128d7ec23441722628054ad417f3258 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caio Bruchert <caio.bruchert@windriver.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:59:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] synce4l.8: refresh man page for DPLL netlink mode and new
 options

The installed synce4l.8 man page had drifted from the code: it documented
only the legacy line/external input-mode model and was missing the DPLL
netlink mode, the external source section, and several configuration
options present in this build.

Refresh the page to describe the current configuration surface:

- Add an operating-modes section (DPLL netlink mode, selected when both
  clock_id and module_name are set, versus command/legacy mode).
- Document the device options clock_id, module_name, dnu_prio and the
  holdover options holdover_tx, holdover_tx_ql and holdover_tx_ext_ql.
- Document the external source section, its input_QL, input_ext_QL,
  external_enable_cmd, external_disable_cmd, source_ports, internal_prio
  and the board_label / panel_label / package_label DPLL pin labels.
- Add the global poll_interval_msec and smc_socket_path options and
  quality-level reference tables for both network options.
- Correct stale option names and defaults (eec_get_state_cmd,
  recover_time default 300, poll_interval_msec range) and note that the
  obsolete input_mode option is accepted but ignored.
- Remove the deprecated external_input_QL / external_input_ext_QL options
  and the line/external input-mode narrative that no longer applies.

Intel's upstream synce4l.8 is frozen at 1.0, so this page also documents
options that are only present with the applied patches on top of upstream
1.1.2; the title and description note the patched build.

Signed-off-by: Caio Bruchert <caio.bruchert@windriver.com>
---
 synce4l.8 | 438 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 323 insertions(+), 115 deletions(-)

diff --git a/synce4l.8 b/synce4l.8
index f9af549..b290f80 100644
--- a/synce4l.8
+++ b/synce4l.8
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 .\" Manpage for synce4l.
 .\" Contact arkadiusz.kubalewski@intel.com or michal.michalik@intel.com to
 .\" correct errors or typos.
-.TH man 8 "27 Oct 2022" "1.0" "synce4l man page"
+.TH man 8 "29 Jul 2025" "1.1.2+stx" "synce4l man page"
 
 .SH NAME
 synce4l \- Synchronous Ethernet (SyncE) controller application
@@ -13,25 +13,81 @@ synce4l -f [file] [-l <num>] [-m] [-q] [-v] [-h]
 synce4l is an implementation of the Synchronous Ethernet (SyncE) protocol
 according to ITU-T Rec. G.8264. The design goal is to provide logic to supported
 hardware by processing Ethernet Synchronization Messaging Channel (ESMC) and
-control Ethernet Equipment Clock (EEC) on Network Card Interface (NIC).
+control Ethernet Equipment Clock (EEC) on a Network Interface Card (NIC).
 .P
-Application can operate in two mutually exclusive modes: line or external.
+Incoming SyncE frames are processed and the best clock source is extracted from
+the link having the best quality level. synce4l configures such "best quality"
+port as the source used to recover the clock for the EEC. The recovered QL is
+then broadcast to all other interfaces. An external frequency source (for
+example a 1PPS input from GPS or another generator) may also be configured; such
+a source participates in the best source selection algorithm for the EEC.
+.P
+The best source selection follows ITU-T Recommendations G.781 and G.8264. Two
+network options are supported: option 1 and option 2.
+.P
+This page documents the StarlingX-patched synce4l build (upstream 1.1.2 plus the
+StarlingX integration patches), so it includes options that are not present in a
+stock upstream 1.1.2 release.
+
+.SH OPERATING MODES
+synce4l controls the EEC on each device using one of two mutually exclusive
+hardware interfaces. The mode is selected per device (per device section) by the
+presence of the \fBclock_id\fR and \fBmodule_name\fR options:
 
 .TP
-External input mode
-If `synce4l` is configured to run in external input mode then EEC needs to
-have external 1PPS source attached (GPS or other generator).
-In this scenario `synce4l` always broadcasts clock quality level (QL) defined
-in configuration file. Additionally, for external input mode incoming SyncE
-frames do not participate in best source selection algorithm for EEC.
+DPLL netlink mode
+Selected when \fBboth\fR \fBclock_id\fR and \fBmodule_name\fR are set in the
+device section. synce4l controls and monitors the EEC through the Linux DPLL
+subsystem (netlink). In this mode the DPLL reports clock state and synce4l drives
+input pin priorities directly; external sources are identified by their DPLL pin
+labels (\fBboard_label\fR, \fBpanel_label\fR or \fBpackage_label\fR). The
+\fBeec_get_state_cmd\fR / \fBeec_*_value\fR and \fBrecover_clock_*_cmd\fR /
+\fBexternal_*_cmd\fR shell-command options are not used in this mode.
 
 .TP
-Line input mode
-In line input mode incoming SyncE frames are processed and best clock source is
-extracted from the link having the best quality level.
-`synce4l` configures such "best quality" port as a source to recover clock for
-EEC. The recovered QL is broadcasted to all other interfaces then.
-An external clock source cannot be used in this mode.
+Command (legacy) mode
+Selected when \fBclock_id\fR or \fBmodule_name\fR is absent. synce4l reads the
+EEC state and controls clock recovery by executing user-supplied shell commands
+(\fBeec_get_state_cmd\fR with the \fBeec_*_value\fR strings, and the
+\fBrecover_clock_enable_cmd\fR / \fBrecover_clock_disable_cmd\fR /
+\fBexternal_enable_cmd\fR / \fBexternal_disable_cmd\fR options).
+
+.SH QUALITY LEVELS
+The following tables list the SyncE quality levels (QL), their selection
+priority and the corresponding SSM / extended SSM codes. A lower priority number
+means higher priority. If extended SSM is not enabled it is implicitly assumed
+to be 0xFF.
+.P
+Network option 1:
+.TS
+box, tab(:);
+l l l l
+l l l l.
+Quality Level:Priority:SSM:Ext SSM
+ePRTC:0:0x2:0x21
+PRTC:1:0x2:0x20
+PRC:2:0x2:0xFF
+SSU-A:3:0x4:0xFF
+SSU-B:4:0x8:0xFF
+EEC1:5:0xB:0xFF
+.TE
+.P
+Network option 2:
+.TS
+box, tab(:);
+l l l l
+l l l l.
+Quality Level:Priority:SSM:Ext SSM
+ePRTC:0:0x1:0x21
+PRTC:1:0x1:0x20
+PRS:2:0x1:0xFF
+STU:3:0x0:0xFF
+ST2:4:0x7:0xFF
+TNC:5:0x4:0xFF
+ST3E:6:0xD:0xFF
+EEC2:7:0xA:0xFF
+PROV:8:0xE:0xFF
+.TE
 
 .SH OPTIONS
 .TP
@@ -53,168 +109,320 @@ print synce4l version and exit
 .TP
 .B \-h
 print this message and exit
+.P
+synce4l requires root privileges since it opens raw sockets.
 
 .SH CONFIGURATION FILE
-Configuration file contains three sections:
+The configuration file contains four kinds of sections, identified by the
+bracket style around the section name:
 .IP -
-global,
+global \- introduced by [global].
 .IP -
-device,
+device \- introduced by [<name>] (angle brackets), e.g. [<synce1>].
 .IP -
-port.
+port \- introduced by [name] (plain brackets), e.g. [eth0].
+.IP -
+external source \- introduced by [{name}] (curly brackets), e.g. [{SMA1}].
+.P
+A device section begins a logical SyncE device. All port and external source
+sections that follow (until the next device section) belong to that device.
+Multiple devices, ports and external sources are supported.
+.P
+Numeric option values may be given in decimal or in C-style hexadecimal
+notation with a 0x prefix (for example, clock_id and the QL options accept
+either form).
 
 .SS Global section
-This section starts with `[global]` keyword. It sets the logging options.
+This section starts with the `[global]` keyword and configures the running
+synce4l instance.
 .RS
-Available options:
 .IP logging_level
 Minimum log level required to appear in a log.
-.P
 .RS
-Defaults to 6, valid values are 0 - 7
+Defaults to 6, valid values are 0 - 7.
 .RE
 .IP message_tag
 Tag reported in a log.
-.IP use_syslog
-Set to 1 if `syslog` should be used.
-.P
+.IP poll_interval_msec
+Sleep time, in milliseconds, between subsequent SyncE clock polls.
 .RS
-Defaults to 1, valid values are 0 or 1
+Defaults to 20, valid values are 1 - 500.
+.RE
+.IP smc_socket_path
+Full path to the AF_UNIX socket file used for external application
+communication (see EXTERNAL API).
+.RS
+Defaults to /run/synce4l_socket.
+.RE
+.IP use_syslog
+Set to 1 if syslog should be used.
+.RS
+Defaults to 1, valid values are 0 or 1.
 .RE
 .IP verbose
 Set to 1 to log extra information.
-.P
 .RS
-Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 or 1
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 or 1.
 .RE
 .RE
 
 .SS Device section
-This section specifies the configuration of a one logical device e.g. 'synce1'.
-The name is defined by the user. The name has no impact for any functionality
-except traces.
-The name must be enclosed in extra angle bracket when defining new device
-section e.g. [<synce1>].
-All ports defined by port sections after the device section will create one
-SyncE device (until next device section).
-.RS
-Available options:
-.IP input_mode
-Set to "line" to enable line input mode, set "external" for external input mode.
+This section specifies the configuration of one logical device, e.g. 'synce1'.
+The name is defined by the user and has no impact on functionality except
+traces. The name must be enclosed in angle brackets, e.g. [<synce1>].
 .P
+The obsolete input_mode option is still accepted for backward compatibility but
+is ignored; the operating mode is selected as described in OPERATING MODES.
 .RS
-Defaults to "line", valid values are "line" or "external"
-.RE
-.IP external_input_QL
-Quality Level (QL) for "external input" mode.
-.P
-.RS
-Valid values specified in ITU-T Recommendations
-.RE
-.IP external_input_ext_QL
-Extended Quality Level for "external input" mode.
-.P
-.RS
-Valid values specified in ITU-T Recommendations
-.RE
 .IP extended_tlv
 Set to 1 to enable extended QL.
-.P
 .RS
-Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 or 1
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 or 1.
 .RE
 .IP network_option
-Network option according to T-REC-G.8264. All devices in SyncE domain
-should have the same option configured.
-.P
+Network option according to ITU-T G.8264. All devices in a SyncE domain should
+have the same option configured.
 .RS
-Defaults to 1, valid values are 1 or 2
+Defaults to 1, valid values are 1 or 2.
 .RE
 .IP recover_time
-Seconds indicating the minimum time to recover from the QL-failed state on the port.
-.P
+Seconds indicating the minimum time to recover from the QL-failed state on a
+port.
 .RS
-Defaults to 60, valid values are 10 - 720
+Defaults to 300, valid values are 10 - 720.
 .RE
-.IP get_eec_state_cmd
-Defines a shell command which will be executed by synce4l to acquire current
-state of a SyncE EEC on the device. Separated command must be provided by the
-user for each device confgured for frequency synchronization. The command shall
-output current state of EEC to stdout, expected values are defined (also by the
-user) with following configuration items:
-eec_holdover_value, eec_locked_ho_value, eec_locked_value,
-eec_freerun_value, eec_invalid_value.
+.IP clock_id
+Clock ID of the EEC-type DPLL in the system. Required, together with
+module_name, to control the EEC through the Linux DPLL subsystem (DPLL netlink
+mode); the presence of both clock_id and module_name is what selects DPLL
+netlink mode.
 .RS
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 - 0xffffffffffffffff.
 .RE
+.IP module_name
+Name of the kernel module that registered the DPLL device in the system.
+Required, together with clock_id, to control the EEC through the Linux DPLL
+subsystem (DPLL netlink mode).
+.RS
+Defaults to unset.
+.RE
+.IP dnu_prio
+DPLL netlink mode only. Input pin priority value assigned when a source is
+marked Do-Not-Use (DNU).
+.RS
+Defaults to 15, valid values are 15 - 0xffff.
+.RE
+.IP holdover_tx
+DPLL netlink mode only. Set to 1 to advertise a holdover quality level (instead
+of DNU) on all ports while the DPLL is in a valid EEC HOLDOVER state. The QL and
+extended QL advertised are taken verbatim from holdover_tx_ql and
+holdover_tx_ext_ql.
+.RS
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 or 1.
+.RE
+.IP holdover_tx_ql
+SSM quality level advertised during EEC holdover when holdover_tx is enabled.
+The value is sent verbatim, including 0 (STU); it is not treated as an unset
+sentinel. Choosing a holdover QL appropriate to the network option is the
+operator's responsibility, as there is no safe built-in default.
+.RS
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 - 15.
+.RE
+.IP holdover_tx_ext_ql
+Extended SSM quality level advertised during EEC holdover when holdover_tx is
+enabled. Applied only when extended_tlv is set.
+.RS
+Defaults to 0xff, valid values are 0 - 255.
+.RE
+.IP eec_get_state_cmd
+Command (legacy) mode only. Shell command executed by synce4l to acquire the
+current state of the SyncE EEC on the device. The command shall output the
+current EEC state to stdout; the expected strings are defined by the
+eec_holdover_value, eec_locked_ho_value, eec_locked_value, eec_freerun_value and
+eec_invalid_value options.
 .IP eec_holdover_value
-Defines a string value expected on stdout stream when EEC is in HOLDOVER state.
-.P
-.RS
-.RE
+String expected on stdout when the EEC is in the HOLDOVER state.
 .IP eec_locked_ho_value
-Defines a string value expected on stdout stream when EEC is in LOCKED HOLDOVER
-state.
-.P
-.RS
-.RE
+String expected on stdout when the EEC is in the LOCKED HOLDOVER state.
 .IP eec_locked_value
-Defines a string value expected on stdout stream when EEC is in LOCKED state.
-.P
-.RS
-.RE
+String expected on stdout when the EEC is in the LOCKED state.
 .IP eec_freerun_value
-Defines a string value expected on stdout stream when EEC is in FREERUN state.
-.P
-.RS
-.RE
+String expected on stdout when the EEC is in the FREERUN state.
 .IP eec_invalid_value
-Defines a string value expected on stdout stream when EEC is in INVALID state.
-.P
+String expected on stdout when the EEC is in the INVALID state.
 .RE
 
 .SS Port section
-Any other section not starting with `<` (e.g. [eth0]) is the port section.
-Multiple port sections are allowed. Each port participates in SyncE
-communication.
+Any section in plain brackets, e.g. [eth0], is a port section. Multiple port
+sections are allowed. Each port participates in SyncE communication.
 .RS
-Available options:
 .IP tx_heartbeat_msec
-Interval between consecutive SyncE frame transmissions (1000ms recommended).
-.P
+Interval between consecutive SyncE frame transmissions (1000 ms recommended).
 .RS
-Defaults to 1000, valid values are 100 - 3000
+Defaults to 1000, valid values are 100 - 3000.
 .RE
 .IP rx_heartbeat_msec
 Interval between consecutive SyncE socket polls (frame receive).
-.P
 .RS
-Defaults to 50, valid values are 10 - 500
+Defaults to 50, valid values are 10 - 500.
 .RE
 .IP recover_clock_enable_cmd
-A shell command which enables PHY port pointed by this Port section as a source
-of frequency for the SyncE EEC on this device (required only in
-"internal input" mode).
-.RS
-.RE
+Command (legacy) mode only. Shell command that enables the PHY port pointed to
+by this port section as a frequency source for the SyncE EEC on this device.
 .IP recover_clock_disable_cmd
-A shell command which disables PHY port pointed by this Port section as a source
-of frequency for the SyncE EEC on this device (required only in
-"internal input" mode).
+Command (legacy) mode only. Shell command that disables the PHY port pointed to
+by this port section as a frequency source for the SyncE EEC on this device.
 .IP allowed_qls
-List of integers containing allowed SSM QLs separated by comma (`,`), other
-received ones would be discarded. If parameter is not provided, all QLs will be
-accepted.
-.P
+List of hexadecimal values of allowed SSM QLs, separated by commas. Received QLs
+not in the list are discarded. If not provided, all QLs are accepted.
 .IP allowed_ext_qls
-List of integers containing allowed extended SSM QLs separated by comma (`,`),
-other received ones would be discarded. If parameter is not provided, all QLs will
-be accepted.
-.P
+List of hexadecimal values of allowed extended SSM QLs, separated by commas.
+Received extended QLs not in the list are discarded. If not provided, all
+extended QLs are accepted.
 .RE
 
+.SS External source section
+Any section in curly brackets, e.g. [{SMA1}], is an external source section.
+Multiple external source sections are allowed. Each external source participates
+in the best source selection algorithm for the EEC.
+.RS
+.IP input_QL
+Quality Level (QL) advertised for this external source.
+.RS
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 - 15 (0x0 - 0xF).
+.RE
+.IP input_ext_QL
+Extended Quality Level advertised for this external source.
+.RS
+Defaults to 0, valid values are 0 - 255 (0x0 - 0xFF).
+.RE
+.IP internal_prio
+Internal source priority used as a tiebreaker; a higher priority (lower value)
+selects a source as better quality when two sources are otherwise of equal
+quality.
+.RS
+Defaults to 128, valid values are 0 - 255.
+.RE
+.IP external_enable_cmd
+Command (legacy) mode only. Shell command that enables the external clock source
+pointed to by this section as a frequency source for the SyncE EEC on this
+device.
+.IP external_disable_cmd
+Command (legacy) mode only. Shell command that disables the external clock
+source pointed to by this section as a frequency source for the SyncE EEC on
+this device.
+.IP source_ports
+Comma-separated list of port names whose transmitted QL should track the QL of
+this external source, allowing the external source QL to be passed through to
+the listed ports.
+.IP board_label
+DPLL netlink mode only. Label of the DPLL pin associated with this external EEC
+input, as registered in the Linux DPLL subsystem.
+.IP panel_label
+DPLL netlink mode only. Label of the DPLL pin associated with this external EEC
+input, as registered in the Linux DPLL subsystem.
+.IP package_label
+DPLL netlink mode only. Label of the DPLL pin associated with this external EEC
+input, as registered in the Linux DPLL subsystem.
+.RS
+When the DPLL subsystem is used, one of board_label, panel_label or
+package_label must be provided, depending on the type of label under which the
+given input is registered in the Linux DPLL subsystem.
+.RE
+.RE
+
+.SH EXAMPLES
+Command (legacy) mode configuration:
+.PP
+.RS
+.nf
+[global]
+logging_level              7
+use_syslog                 0
+verbose                    1
+message_tag                [synce4l]
+smc_socket_path            /run/synce4l_socket
+
+[<synce1>]
+network_option             1
+extended_tlv               1
+recover_time               20
+eec_get_state_cmd          cat /sys/class/net/eth0/device/dpll_0_state
+eec_holdover_value         4
+eec_locked_ho_value        3
+eec_locked_value           2
+eec_freerun_value          1
+eec_invalid_value          0
+
+[eth0]
+tx_heartbeat_msec          1000
+rx_heartbeat_msec          500
+recover_clock_enable_cmd   echo 1 0 > /sys/class/net/eth0/device/phy/synce
+recover_clock_disable_cmd  echo 0 0 > /sys/class/net/eth0/device/phy/synce
+allowed_qls                0x2,0x4,0x8
+allowed_ext_qls            0x20,0x21
+
+[{SMA1}]
+external_enable_cmd        echo 2 1 > /sys/class/net/enp1s0f0/device/ptp/ptp*/pins/SMA1
+external_disable_cmd       echo 0 1 > /sys/class/net/enp1s0f0/device/ptp/ptp*/pins/SMA1
+input_QL                   0x2
+input_ext_QL               0x20
+internal_prio              0
+.fi
+.RE
+.PP
+Linux DPLL (netlink) mode configuration:
+.PP
+.RS
+.nf
+[global]
+logging_level              7
+use_syslog                 0
+verbose                    1
+message_tag                [synce4l]
+smc_socket_path            /run/synce4l_socket
+
+[<synce1>]
+network_option             1
+extended_tlv               1
+recover_time               20
+clock_id                   0xaabbccffffccbbaa
+module_name                ice
+holdover_tx                1
+holdover_tx_ql             0xb
+holdover_tx_ext_ql         0xff
+
+[eth0]
+tx_heartbeat_msec          1000
+rx_heartbeat_msec          500
+allowed_qls                0x2,0x4,0x8
+allowed_ext_qls            0x20,0x21
+
+[{SMA1}]
+board_label                SMA1
+input_QL                   0x2
+input_ext_QL               0x20
+internal_prio              0
+.fi
+.RE
+
+.SH EXTERNAL API
+synce4l can be queried and controlled by an external application over the
+AF_UNIX socket configured by the global smc_socket_path option. Messages are
+exchanged as a stream of TLV (Type-Length-Value) records; every stream is
+terminated by a record of type MSG_END_MARKER. The response uses the same TLV
+format. The message types and structures are defined in synce_external_api.h.
+
 .SH BUGS
 No known bugs.
 
